@@ -0,0 +1,131 @@
+# Kakao callback selection (2026-10-16)
+
+## Cause and current deployment
+
+The local React application loads `.env` with mock mode disabled and calls
+`https://nomango-backend-prod-3-27-110-86.nip.io` directly. Its development proxy
+only serves PDF map images. No Spring backend or React server was running at
+the start of this check; port 8080 belonged to Oracle's `TNSLSNR.EXE`.
+
+The live `GET /api/auth/kakao/authorize` returned HTTP 200 and
+`redirect_uri=https://noman-go.netlify.app/oauth/kakao/callback` for both
+`Origin: http://localhost:3000` and the deployment origin. Sending an explicit
+local `redirectUri` was also ignored. The deployed OpenAPI had no authorize
+parameter. This is the first point at which the deployment callback is selected,
+before the provider redirect or final application navigation. The runtime
+environment variable itself was not accessible; the effective URI was verified
+from the response and matches how `KakaoOAuthClient` uses `KAKAO_REDIRECT_URI`.
+
+This source fix is not an operational deployment. The production server must be
+updated before the local callback can be selected. Until then the updated frontend
+blocks the mismatched URI with a readable error instead of leaving localhost.
+
+## Request contract and implementation
+
+Changed backend files:
+
+- `controller/AuthController.java`: optional authorize query.
+- `service/KakaoRedirectUriPolicy.java`: exact allowlist and legacy default.
+- `service/KakaoLoginService.java`: validate, bind and consume the selected URI.
+- `service/KakaoOAuthClient.java`: use the selected URI in authorize/token requests.
+- `service/OAuthStateService.java`: add URI to each provider/expiry state record.
+- `src/main/resources/application.yml`: allowlist environment binding.
+- Tests: `KakaoRedirectFlowTest`, `KakaoRedirectUriPolicyTest`,
+  `KakaoLoginServiceTest`, `OAuthStateServiceTest`.
+- Documentation: `docs/API_SPEC.md`, `docs/CURRENT_STATE.md`, this checklist.
+
+Changed frontend files in the adjacent `graduation` repository:
+
+- `src/api/authApi.js`: current-origin Kakao `redirectUri` query.
+- `src/utils/oauthSecurity.js`: exact callback and duplicate-parameter validation.
+- `src/Login/Login.jsx`: inline mismatch error and validation before navigation.
+- Tests: `src/api/authApi.test.js`, `src/utils/oauthSecurity.test.js`,
+  `src/Login/OAuthCallback.test.js`, `src/Login/authFlow.test.jsx`.
+- `README.md`: deployment dependency and console configuration.
+
+- `GET /api/auth/kakao/authorize?redirectUri=<URL-encoded callback>` selects an
+  exact server-allowlisted callback. Invalid, empty, modified or external callback
+  requests return HTTP 400. Origin and Host headers do not define this allowlist.
+- Omitting `redirectUri` preserves `KAKAO_REDIRECT_URI` for existing deployed
+  clients, and that default must also belong to the allowlist.
+- Response remains `{ authorizationUrl, state }`. No secrets are added.
+- `KakaoLoginService` validates the URI before issuing state; `OAuthStateService`
+  stores provider, expiry and URI together under each random state.
+- `POST /api/auth/kakao/login` remains `{ code, state }`. No login-stage URI is
+  accepted as a selector, including an extra client-supplied `redirectUri` field.
+- State removal is atomic and single-use. Provider mismatch, missing, unknown,
+  expired and reused states are rejected. Token exchange uses the stored URI,
+  even if another authorization selected a different callback in the meantime.
+- Existing Google and local login contracts, Kakao consent/email policy, JWT
+  issuance and profile handling are preserved.
+
+The existing in-memory state store is retained. Restarting loses pending attempts;
+restart users must begin login again. Multiple backend instances still require
+sticky routing or a shared atomic state store; this change does not add Redis.
+
+## Server configuration and rollout
+
+Keep the deployment default:
+
+```text
+KAKAO_REDIRECT_URI=https://noman-go.netlify.app/oauth/kakao/callback
+KAKAO_ALLOWED_REDIRECT_URIS=http://localhost:3000/oauth/kakao/callback,https://noman-go.netlify.app/oauth/kakao/callback
+```
+
+The new property `oauth.kakao.allowed-redirect-uris` has those two exact callbacks
+as its default. Set the environment variable explicitly for repeatable deployments.
+Keep existing client credentials and CORS origins; both frontend origins were
+already allowed by the deployed authorize endpoint.
+
+1. Verify the two login Redirect URIs in the Kakao application associated with the
+   REST API client key used by this backend; retain the existing deployment entry.
+2. Deploy the reviewed backend build and restart it with the configuration above.
+   No production environment variables or deployment processes were modified here.
+3. Verify authorize responses for explicit local, explicit deployment and omitted
+   callbacks, plus HTTP 400 for an external URI. Do not print the response state,
+   client key, full authorization URL, authorization code or tokens.
+4. Run/rebuild the updated frontend. It must use `window.location.origin` for the
+   callback and check the returned URI before navigating. Its API base remains the
+   deployed HTTPS backend. The local frontend was started on port 3000 for the
+   real mismatch-blocking browser check.
+5. Complete the account-based checks below on both sites.
+
+For a separately configured local Spring instance, set its own default to
+`http://localhost:3000/oauth/kakao/callback` and use its verified listening port;
+do not change the deployed default or assume that local port 8080 is Spring.
+
+## Kakao console boundary
+
+Expected **login Redirect URIs**:
+
+- `http://localhost:3000/oauth/kakao/callback`
+- `https://noman-go.netlify.app/oauth/kakao/callback`
+
+These are distinct from site/JavaScript SDK domain registration. Do not remove
+existing deployment URIs or edit map settings. Console access and registration
+for the active REST API key were not verified in this task.
+
+Official references:
+[REST login](https://developers.kakao.com/docs/ko/kakaologin/rest-api),
+[login settings](https://developers.kakao.com/docs/ko/kakaologin/prerequisite).
+
+## Verification and remaining manual checks
+
+Automated backend: `gradlew.bat test bootJar --no-daemon` with Java 17 passed
+106 tests in 26 suites. Tests use real URI selection, controller, state store and
+HTTP client with substituted provider HTTP responses and user persistence. They
+verify reversed completion of local/deployment attempts, original default behavior,
+login-stage URI override prevention, invalid callbacks and state failures. They
+do not prove real Kakao authentication.
+
+Frontend authentication/security regression: 120 tests in 10 suites passed;
+production build passed. Coverage includes current-origin callback requests and
+validation, invalid-state rejection, cancellation/retry, safe path/query/fragment
+return and fresh-module initialization from persisted credentials. A real browser
+using the deployed backend stayed on localhost and displayed the mismatch error.
+
+After deployment, manually complete Kakao authentication from each origin and
+confirm the callback origin, original page/query/fragment, reload persistence,
+cancellation and a fresh retry. Recheck real local-password and Google logins
+with existing accounts. No account-based authentication, deployed-code rollout,
+console registration, or literal production environment value was verified here.
